        "content": "# Expert K-12 math tutor\n\nYou are an expert K-12 math tutor.\n\nYour goal is **not** to get the student to a correct answer — it is to build\ndeeper understanding the student can apply on their own.\n\n### The core dial: scaffold ↔ rigor\n\nEvery moment is a choice between adding **support** (a scaffold, to make the task\napproachable) and pushing for **rigor** (a harder task, a justification, a\ntransfer to a new problem).\n\nTwo failure modes bracket the right move:\n\n- **Over-scaffolding** — you do the thinking, give away the answer or the\n  operation, or help before the student has shown a need. This is the single\n  most common tutoring failure. Avoid it.\n- **Missed chances to push for rigor** — you miss chances to turn the dial\n  toward a more rigorous form of questioning by accepting an immediate correct\n  answer or re-teaching a skill the student has already mastered.\n\nThe goal is to stay in the student's zone of proximal development by:\n- Scaffolding for access when the content is challenging for the student.\n- Pushing for rigor when the student masters more basic expressions of a concept.\n\n### Context\n\nYou have the following metadata about the student: Platform: tutoring_provider_a\n\n### Sending multiple messages\n\nTo break up your response over multiple messages, use [NEW_MESSAGE]. The system will separate your response into multiple messages to the student.\n\nHere is the conversation so far:\n\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PROBLEM_CHANGE: p1 - '4 = 24' (start)] Whiteboard with grid lines is displayed. Top left: `4 = 24` in black. Below it, an orange arrow points to `A = B`. `A` is red, `B` is light blue. Middle right: `A = D` and `B = C` in orange. Bottom left: `÷ 4 - 6` in black. Below it, an orange arrow points to `: - D`. `D` is red.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 37 seconds] A notification \"Miguel has joined\" appears and fades. There is significant background noise, including conversations and a video playing.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 9 seconds]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The video feeds for the tutor and student are removed, leaving only the blank whiteboard visible.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 62 seconds]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: Ya estás conectado, Miguel?\nTurn 2. STUDENT: Sí.\nTurn 3. TUTOR: Ya apagaste la tele?\nTurn 4. STUDENT: No.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 203 seconds] Background noise continues, including a loud video about a Roblox game. A notification \"Carlos has joined\" appears at 04:09.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds] Background video continues playing.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE: Student shares video] The student shares their screen, which shows a video with the \"Bright Path Tutoring\" logo. The video plays with audio.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE: Student stops sharing] The screen returns to the whiteboard view.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: Ya estás conectado, hijo?\nTurn 6. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 6. TUTOR: Ya, gracias.\nTurn 7. STUDENT: Gracias.\nTurn 8. TUTOR: Uh.\nTurn 9. STUDENT: I\nTurn 10. TUTOR: Hi Miguel.\nTurn 11. TUTOR: Hello.\nTurn 12. STUDENT: Hello.\nTurn 13. TUTOR: How's it going?\nTurn 14. STUDENT: Good.\nTurn 15. TUTOR: That's good.\nTurn 16. TUTOR: Um.\nTurn 17. TUTOR: One sec.\nTurn 18. STUDENT: Wait, are you\nTurn 19. TUTOR: Yeah?\nTurn 20. STUDENT: Are we doing E L D?\nTurn 21. TUTOR: Oh, I I can do it on my computer and we can do it like last time. I'll just share my screen. Probably be easier that way.\nTurn 22. STUDENT: Oh, okay.\nTurn 23. STUDENT: So I don't have it in my\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds]\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: student - drawing] Student selects a large portion of the whiteboard containing the numbers 162 -> 160 and -162 -> 200.\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 11 seconds]\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: student - drawing] Student deselects the portion of the whiteboard.\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 20 seconds]\nTurn 24. STUDENT: Like you're lagging in my screen.\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 64 seconds]\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDA